# Model attribution and license notice

AvaPardaz downloads the following third-party model at CI/runtime setup; the binary weights are intentionally not committed to this repository.

- Model: WeSpeaker ECAPA-TDNN512-LM (VoxCeleb ECAPA512 large-margin model)
- Upstream project/model publisher: WeSpeaker
- Source: https://huggingface.co/Wespeaker/wespeaker-ecapa-tdnn512-LM
- Pinned upstream revision: a2f3dcb1c8702caccc7a55ceb57f5e8d1842112b
- Declared upstream license: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
- License text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

The upstream model card states that the model is trained on VoxCeleb2 Dev and points to the WeSpeaker project and its publications. This repository distributes no model weights; the CI downloader obtains the pinned upstream file directly and verifies its SHA-256 before use.

AvaPardaz adds a separate Kaldi-style FBANK frontend, inference integration and L2 normalization. These are integration changes, not a claim that the model has been retrained or validated for Persian. The source model is not yet approved for production speaker diarization: Persian DER/JER and false merge/split evaluations remain required.

Please retain this notice and the upstream attribution when redistributing a build that includes or downloads this model.
